In the early years of iPhone launches, long lines would form at Apple Stores around the world, but those queues gradually became a thing of the past amid the rise of online pre-orders. At least, until the iPhone Duo launched today.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-Store-Austin-Texas-iPhone-Duo-Launch-Day.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072537" /><em>Apple Domain NORTHSIDE in Austin, Texas today</em></div><br/>
<a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/10/iphone-duo-arrives-at-apple-store-locations-worldwide/">iPhone Duo fever</a> is real today, with queues having formed at many Apple Stores around the world, based on comments and photos shared <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/waiting-in-line-thread-which-store-and-what-time-are-you-lining-up-merged.2492032/">on the MacRumors Forums</a> and social media platforms. Anywhere from dozens to hundreds of people lined up at the stores on Friday morning or even a day or two earlier for a chance to buy the iPhone Duo.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's CEO John Ternus and retail chief Deirdre O'Brien visited Apple Domain NORTHSIDE in Austin, Texas, likely because F1's U.S. Grand Prix is taking place there this weekend and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/22/f1-apple-tv-dolby-atmos/">Apple TV is the exclusive U.S. streaming partner of F1</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Apple's marketing chief Greg Joswiak and vice president of retail stores Vanessa Trigub greeted customers at Apple Fifth Avenue in New York City. <br/>
<br/>
<p><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/t/Cbq-DlQfaBzaBiL2M8iwPb-tYxA=/800x0/article-new/2026/10/Apple-Domain-NORTHSIDE-Austin-Deirdre-O-Brien-and-John-Ternus-welcome-customers-261023-scaled.jpg" alt=""></p><p><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/23/iphone-duo-long-lines-at-apple-stores/#gallery-1072514-1">View all 16 photos in the full article →</a></p><br/>
<br/>
Apple said the iPhone Duo would be available <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-stores-limited-iphone-duo-for-walk-in/">on a "limited" basis for walk-in customers</a> in the U.S. and select other countries today, but it expected supply to sell out quickly due to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/16/apple-iphone-duo-demand-extraordinary/">"extraordinary" pre-order demand</a> for the device. Indeed, some locations have now sold through their walk-in inventory for launch day, so your mileage may vary.<br/>
<br/>
Apple Store pickup was very briefly an option when iPhone Duo pre-orders began last Friday, but the system has been unavailable ever since. In most countries, <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-iphone/iphone-duo">Apple's online store</a> says to check back on Saturday, October 24 regarding Apple Store pickup, but we do not know exactly what time reservations will resume at, so make sure to check Apple's website early and often tomorrow if you are still trying to secure an iPhone Duo.<br/>
<br/>
